yoyo run "echo a b" now prints a b and exits 0. Before the fix it failed with sh: 1: echo a b: not found and exit 127. The fix is committed as b3a2ed90 with Part of #1009, and build, all tests, clippy and fmt pass.

The rule: in src/dispatch_sub.rs, if run gets exactly one argument, that argument goes to the shell unchanged as a command line. With two or more arguments, run still uses the old quoting, so yoyo run echo "a  b" still keeps its double space. Bare yoyo run is untouched.

Measured before and after, from the built binary:

| invocation | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| run "echo a b" | 127 | 0, a b |
| run "exit 3" | 127 (same bug) | 3 |
| run "false" | 1 | 1 |
| run echo "a  b", run echo hi, bare run | 0 | 0, unchanged |
| run "./my script.sh" | 0, ran the script | 127, ./my: not found |
| run "'./my script.sh'" | 127 | 0, ran the script |

The last two rows are the trade. A single argument that is a path with a space in it is now split into words by the shell, the same way sh -c would. Quoting the path inside the argument runs it. A test pins this, and the commit body explains why the trade is still right.

• **"exit 3" was broken too:** your plan said `"exit 3"` "must still exit 3", but at HEAD it exited 127 for the same reason. The new test expects 3, which is the correct value, not the old recording.
• **Tests:** I added four tests in `tests/integration.rs` that run the built binary. They normalise the `(Nms)` timing so whole outputs can be compared exactly.
• **Positive control:** I sent single-argument input back through the old quoting, in one mutate→test→restore command. The three single-argument tests failed by name, the multi-argument test stayed green, and all four passed after the restore.
• Size gate: `dispatch_sub.rs` was already 95 lines past its size limit before this change, so my first, longer comment failed the module-size test. I cut the comment at the branch to two lines rather than raise the limit. The full explanation of the trade is in the commit body.
• **Docs:** I added a sentence to the yoyo run row in docs/src/usage/commands.md.
• **Issue #1009:** I marked the `run` row of the table fixed, with the commit, and left the other rows as they were (checked with the `grep` from the plan). I also posted a comment with the before/after table that names watch as the next member under the same rule. The issue is still open.

